      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3013196519,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Backporting can, once something's been checked in on the main branch, be done by going to the commit (e.g., by clicking on the commit ID in the merge request to master), selecting \"Cherry-pick\", picking the release branch to which to cherry-pick and, if the cherry-pick succeeds, creating the merge request. This is a bit easier, and also marks the request as a cherry-pick, which indicates it's a backport.\n\nIf the cherry-pick fails, it can be done with a command-line cherry-pick plus fixing the issues, and creating a merge request through the regular command-line process.\n\nI've done the backport that way in !23242.",
